Life is not meant to be easy my child, but take courage: it can be delightful.
George Bernard Shaw's line, the first part of which is iconic in this country thanks to the late Malcolm Fraser, offers solace in the wake of the Trent Bridge Disaster. For in sport, without defeats and setbacks along the way the victories wouldn't count for much. When they do come, they are the more delightful for the struggle that went before.
